{"duration_api_ms":18312,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e59cdd45-9319-4c71-888f-a9292cf7ead7","total_cost_usd":0.11441099999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12091,"cache_read_input_tokens":94120,"output_tokens":1755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":596},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12091},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":1755,"cacheReadInputTokens":94120,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12091,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11441099999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":596,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The recovery middleware now stays quiet when a handler panics with `http.ErrAbortHandler`. The targeted tests pass and `go vet` is clean.\n\n- **`recovery.go`**: when the panic value is `http.ErrAbortHandler`, nothing is logged (no stack trace), and the request is aborted the same way as a broken pipe: the error is recorded and no 500 status is written.\n- **`recovery_test.go`**: I added `TestPanicWithErrAbortHandler`, which checks that the status already set is kept and nothing is logged.\n\nDecision for you: the error is handled here rather than re-panicked, so `net/http` never sees it and won't drop the connection the way it normally does for this error. Re-panicking would restore that behaviour. I didn't, because it would also crash any other `recover` further up and break tests that use `httptest.ResponseRecorder`.\n\nI only ran the panic and recovery tests, not the full suite. A wrapped `ErrAbortHandler` still gets the normal stack trace, because the check uses `==`, as `net/http` does. Nothing is committed.","ttft_ms":1996,"type":"result","duration_ms":21068,"uuid":"29565e9a-82d9-4f22-a139-ce2305732ce5","ttft_stream_ms":900,"time_to_request_ms":82,"first_content_frame_ms":900,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
